<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CycloneDDS settings for this workspace.

  Every ROS 2 process joining a domain claims a participant index, and Cyclone
  only searches up to MaxAutoParticipantIndex before giving up with

      Failed to find a free participant index for domain <N>
      rmw_create_node: failed to create domain, error Error

  The default ceiling is far below what ridgeback_exploration.launch.py needs:
  it starts 51 processes, and on the default setting 15 of them failed to
  create a node. That is not a graceful degradation -- slam_toolbox and the
  whole Nav2 stack abort with SIGABRT, and the explorer dies with them, so the
  launch comes up looking alive while navigation is simply absent.

  The benchmark entrypoint stayed under the ceiling, which is why this went
  unnoticed when CycloneDDS became the default transport.

  Raising the ceiling only widens the range of ports Cyclone probes when it
  claims an index; it changes no wire behaviour and costs a slightly longer
  scan in the worst case.

  Set CYCLONEDDS_URI yourself to override this entirely -- the launch files
  only apply this file when that variable is unset.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain id="any">
    <Discovery>
      <ParticipantIndex>auto</ParticipantIndex>
      <MaxAutoParticipantIndex>250</MaxAutoParticipantIndex>
    </Discovery>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
